      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Anthropic API key is injected **into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts**. \n\nThe page emphasizes that the key is never held in the Hub\u0027s own process environment. Instead, a local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it only into the spawned child process\u0027s environment. This design prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the credential by inspecting its own environment variables.\n\nThe same scoping model applies to the Query agent process as well \u2014 it receives the credential through environment variable injection at spawn, not inherited from the Hub.",
